WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:13.630
People always like to ask me, what is it that
a producer does? I like to reply, I produce.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:20.030
And that doesn't mean I just pay for it,
though I do. I'm the one who gives birth to

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:24.050
it all. It's what I've always wanted to do.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.300
It's what I've always done.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.180
Well tell him, if he can't write a song that sounds like

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:34.360
Andrew Lloyd Webber, I'll call someone else.
I'll call Andy fucking Weber, That's who, Carl.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.350
Ma'am, we're going to need you to push now.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:40.970
I got to go. Just get it done. Hey.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.680
I've won nine Tonys.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:46.450
I've given birth to 34 Broadway shows.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:53.900
But if someone asks me what my favorite thing
I've ever made is, Mamma mia! Hands down,

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:58.490
changed the trajectory of my whole career.
That's a joke.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.830
Producers can be funny. People don't realize
that.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:05.580
I'm your mommy. I'll protect you for the

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.320
rest of your life.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:22.990
Hey, Carl, tell him the song should be called
The Rest of Your Life.

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:31.820
It's about a parent imagining a life for
their child.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:33.710
The thing no one tells you when

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:40.050
you first start is how rewarding producing
can be. Or...

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.690
How dangerous.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.990
But I should surprise- I know who you are.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:48.900
This is so incredibly exciting to be invited

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:53.310
into the inner sanctum. Like this. Watching
you three work.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:58.090
I imagine it's like being inside that documentary.
Watching Paul McCartney write Get back.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:02.040
Yeah. That's why they call us the Rolling
Stones of true crime.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.060
No, it's the-

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:03.630
Beatles, I was kidding.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:09.410
And thank you for yesterday for stopping me
from pleading guilty to Ben's murder.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:14.310
Well, we know that you were just trying to
protect Dickie, your son.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.250
And thank you for bailing me out.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:17.890
I paid your bail.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:22.410
Yes, but when they say they didn't take Amex,
I hope you find your visa.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:26.280
Anything for you, Mi amore. My peapod.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.540
My little cuddle pops.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:32.070
Oh-

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.480
Is this what this looks like?

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:35.470
You don't call Tobert cuddle pups.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.740
I have a hard enough time calling him
Tobert.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:41.700
The documentary guy. Are you and he?

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.080
Oh, nice.

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.130
Thanks, I know. Right?

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.640
So, are we sure about Donna?

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:52.920
On opening night? Donna got her hands on an
early review, and it was a pan, a massacre.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.300
The harshest review in the history.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:58.320
I have had, like, six heart attacks this
season, Charles. Can we move past the shitty

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.060
review and just recap what we know?

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:07.020
Okay, so Donna can't let her son's first show
be a bomb due to Ben, so she shreds the

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:12.270
review, finds the rat poison, makes a
poisonous cookie, and gives it to him.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:17.460
A cookie she knows that he can't resist due to
his deep-seated eating disorder.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:24.400
And in fact it was my unhealthy relationship to dips that
helped us crack it.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.980
Leave me alone. I'm happy.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:27.460
I'll get help.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:33.070
But the poison didn't kill Ben, so Donna
takes things a step further. She pushes him

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:35.790
down the elevator shaft at Oliver's after
party.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:40.590
Admittedly, it's a pretty drastic step for
her. She had to have been-

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:40.600
sick.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:53.530
She is sick.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.210
And if she only has a limited amount

00:03:55.210 --> 00:04:01.660
of time to ensure her son's future, I tell
you, a mother will do almost anything.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:06.760
It's good, but it's thin. We don't have
anything tying Donna to the push. We need a

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.740
confession on tape.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:10.240
It's what we do.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.190
And on opening night.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:17.080
Okay, let's go over the plan. Let's start
with the bouquet of flowers.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:17.970
Can we tweak these?

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.720
Yeah, I did these really fast.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.660
The Oliver lines on card three, I think I
should take them.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:23.920
You don't think I can say those?

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.870
Oh, no, you could, but I think I can do more
with it.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:26.230
In what way?

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:26.750
How could you do.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:29.830
Well, just it needs to be so real and so
believable. And I have a little more

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:30.580
experience at it.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:31.810
Is it always like this?

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:33.550
This is us on fire.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:34.970
Hey.

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:37.700
Do you know when you're going to tell Dickie?

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:44.750
I just want to get through opening night, and
then I'm going to tell him right afterwards.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:47.150
Oh, yay!

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:48.530
That was a weird thing to fist bump on.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.540
Yeah, it was odd.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:57.090
Oh, Dickie showed me something when he came
to visit me after my arrest, I have it.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:05:00.830
You know what? I think we should lose all
your lines on card nine. I mean, if we want

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:05.090
Donna to confess before curtain, we need
cuts, and you tend to milk your stuff.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.310
Me? Milk my stuff?

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:11.420
Oh, that's right, that's what I do. Yep, I
milk everything. Oh, look at me. Oh, I'm

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:16.490
milking bossy the cow. Milk, milk, milk. Oh,
look at all the milk I'm getting.

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:17.360
Okay, you got a point.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:24.500
Dickie was worried that this might implicate
me, but might this tie Donna to the push?

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:31.210
What? Did I do good?

